sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Admin as Administrator
    participant IdP as Identity Provider<br/>(Keycloak / Okta / etc.)
    participant GrantTool as polar-admin-grant<br/>(holds its own Polar cert --<br/>see admin_bootstrap_identity.mmd)
    participant Cassini as Cassini broker
    participant CredAgentCon as Credentials Agent<br/>(consumer -- high trust)
    participant Graph as Neo4j

    Note over Admin,Graph: Phase 0 -- Admin provisions the user in the IdP<br/>(may already exist -- shown for completeness)

    Admin->>IdP: Provision user account<br/>(or confirm an existing one)
    activate IdP
    IdP-->>Admin: Account created/confirmed
    deactivate IdP

    Admin->>IdP: Query the account for its exact<br/>identity claim value (e.g. preferred_username) --<br/>must be the SAME claim cert-issuer is<br/>configured to extract for this issuer, or the<br/>grant below will silently never match the<br/>token this user actually presents later
    activate IdP
    IdP-->>Admin: Exact claim value
    deactivate IdP

    Note over Admin,Graph: Repeatable. Ordinary, mTLS-authenticated<br/>Cassini traffic -- no different in kind from<br/>any other agent's publish.

    Admin->>GrantTool: Run tool with arguments<br/>(grant: target_identity, permissions --<br/>or revoke: serial, reason)
    activate GrantTool
    GrantTool->>Cassini: Connect using the admin's own<br/>Polar client cert (mTLS)
    activate Cassini

    alt Granting permissions
        GrantTool->>Cassini: Publish { target_identity, permissions,<br/>granted_by, timestamp } to<br/>credentials-grants topic
    else Revoking a certificate
        GrantTool->>Cassini: Publish { serial, reason, revoked_by,<br/>timestamp } to<br/>credentials-revocations topic<br/>(uniform for human- and<br/>workload-issued certs alike)
    end
    deactivate GrantTool

    Cassini->>CredAgentCon: Deliver message
    deactivate Cassini
    activate CredAgentCon
    CredAgentCon->>Graph: Write durable record<br/>(Grant node, or mark a<br/>Certificate node revoked)
    activate Graph
    Graph-->>CredAgentCon: Written
    deactivate Graph
    deactivate CredAgentCon
